| !Run for !Tube - browse YouTube on RISC OS and play videos in Reel
| !RunImage is a UnixLib program (Absolute, AIF): it needs SharedUnixLibrary
| and ARMEABISupport (PackMan), and AcornSSL (RISC OS 5.28 or later) for
| https. Videos play in Reel (riscos-ffmpeg), which the Filer must have seen.
Set Tube$Dir <Obey$Dir>
IconSprites <Tube$Dir>.!Sprites
RMEnsure SharedUnixLibrary 1.16 IfThere System:Modules.SharedULib Then RMLoad System:Modules.SharedULib
RMEnsure SharedUnixLibrary 1.16 Error Tube needs SharedUnixLibrary 1.16 or later. Install it with PackMan.
RMEnsure ARMEABISupport 0 IfThere System:Modules.ARMEABISupport Then RMLoad System:Modules.ARMEABISupport
RMEnsure ARMEABISupport 0 Error Tube needs the ARMEABISupport module. Install it with PackMan.
RMEnsure AcornSSL 0 IfThere System:Modules.Network.URL.AcornSSL Then RMLoad System:Modules.Network.URL.AcornSSL
RMEnsure AcornSSL 0 Error Tube needs the AcornSSL module (RISC OS 5.28 or later) for secure connections.
| The program is small; its memory for lists and pictures is in a dynamic
| area ("Tube Heap").
WimpSlot -min 2048K -max 2048K
Run <Tube$Dir>.!RunImage %*0
